{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkY3tiBEudwjjsrAf36N","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016GFxyxkDTht4rURbJmLD8o","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"working":"Start, after the clef and two sharps: a two-note 16th group high on the staff, read as E5–D5. Next come an A4 quarter, two A4 8ths, then A3 (ledger line below), A4, A4–G4, A3, G4. That is bar 51: (E5 D5), A4 quarter, A4 A4 8ths, A3 A4 (A4 G4) A3 G4. Barline. Next, four three-note 16th groups: two around F#4–G4–A4, then two starting lower, D4–E4–F#4. After them come a G4 quarter, an 8th rest and an E4 8th with a tie into the next bar. That is bar 52. Barline. Next: E4 8th, dotted F#4 16th with an E4 32nd, D4 8th tied to a D4 8th, dotted E4 16th with a D4 32nd, C#4 8th (ledger line), G4 8th. That is bar 53. Barline. Next: a 16th rest, three F#4 16ths with dots or strokes under them, then a group of A3 (ledger line), D4, D4, D4. That is the start of bar 54: rest, F#4 ×3, (A3 D4) D4 D4. The line stops there. The rest of bar 54, from (D4 B3) B3 B3 onward, must be on the next line. So the line runs from the start of bar 51 to partway through bar 54. I found nothing that contradicts the edition.","right":true,"insights":"This line was fairly easy to match. Bar 53's dotted-16th and 32nd figures with the tied D4s are distinctive, and so are bar 54's 16th rest and repeated F#4s. Each confirmed the bar before it. The hardest part was the first group, which is crowded against the clef, and the cut-off end of bar 54. Seeing the start of the next line would have confirmed where bar 54 continues."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5904,"cache_read_input_tokens":523,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5904},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fd9de6ce-00fe-40a5-80cc-714f77481a2e","uuid":"d9dd0b31-dad3-447f-8590-791b6eb53384","timestamp":"2026-11-05T22:02:55.543Z","request_id":"req_011CgkY3tHPEDwMaQD9TUCA5","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_016GFxyxkDTht4rURbJmLD8o":{"working":"Start, after the clef and two sharps: a two-note 16th group high on the staff, read as E5–D5. Next come an A4 quarter, two A4 8ths, then A3 (ledger line below), A4, A4–G4, A3, G4. That is bar 51: (E5 D5), A4 quarter, A4 A4 8ths, A3 A4 (A4 G4) A3 G4. Barline. Next, four three-note 16th groups: two around F#4–G4–A4, then two starting lower, D4–E4–F#4. After them come a G4 quarter, an 8th rest and an E4 8th with a tie into the next bar. That is bar 52. Barline. Next: E4 8th, dotted F#4 16th with an E4 32nd, D4 8th tied to a D4 8th, dotted E4 16th with a D4 32nd, C#4 8th (ledger line), G4 8th. That is bar 53. Barline. Next: a 16th rest, three F#4 16ths with dots or strokes under them, then a group of A3 (ledger line), D4, D4, D4. That is the start of bar 54: rest, F#4 ×3, (A3 D4) D4 D4. The line stops there. The rest of bar 54, from (D4 B3) B3 B3 onward, must be on the next line. So the line runs from the start of bar 51 to partway through bar 54. I found nothing that contradicts the edition.","right":true,"insights":"This line was fairly easy to match. Bar 53's dotted-16th and 32nd figures with the tied D4s are distinctive, and so are bar 54's 16th rest and repeated F#4s. Each confirmed the bar before it. The hardest part was the first group, which is crowded against the clef, and the cut-off end of bar 54. Seeing the start of the next line would have confirmed where bar 54 continues."}}}
